"The Library is technically located in the system of Gregari."
"The Library's current state began when Links plunged it into a hiatus to save it."
"Someone meant the Library to wither without Librarians, and sabotage lies behind its fall."
"Links's own systems carry an infection that leaves gaps in his memory."
"The Library's branches include Combat, Horticultural, Culinary, Alchemical, Medicinal and Crafting."
"Other branches include the Bardic Musical Branch and the Academy."
"Each branch waits in another dimension and is pulled back when its requirements are met."
"A branch opens once its books and items are retrieved and its mana and energy are met."
"A branch also needs a patronage level and a Librarian strength before it opens."
"Opening a branch can go wrong, and the medical and alchemical branch turned dangerous on opening."
"Keys are tiny sprite-like Library inhabitants, loyal to the Library, who guard its branches."
"Many Library books are overdue, some for centuries, lost in burrows and houses across worlds."
"A book's holder hears a return alert when the Library reopens and calls its books home."
"The Library charges fines for late and damaged books, and every Librarian has loved fining."
"The Library waives fines for a few weeks after it reopens, and then fines in earnest."
"The Library pays its staff in Universal Library Currency, ULC, held in a Library account."
"Malachite shards open the Library's doors, and the Library stores them as power."
"The Library feeds and shelters anyone who comes to it in need."
"Security golems kill anyone who spills the blood of Library workers or patrons on Library ground."
"The Library has golems of many kinds: kitchen, worker, security and supervisory."
"The Library gives its staff a translator, which stumbles on idioms like rain check."
"The Library can reshape itself on a whim, and swallow damage by briefly changing shape."
"The Library holds chaos books, which must be cleansed before they can be opened."
"The Library has pillars deep below it, and one, Ashiron, holds a soul bomb that threatens all."
"The Library has a hospital wing, guest quarters, a kitchen, and the Librarian's office."
"The cosmic dragons, the cosmicisodracus, made the Library, first as one big room."
"The Library is built on the dragon form that Drevicia, a cosmicisodracus, sacrificed."
"One of Drevicia's line can take up the Library's connection and become the Library."
"Whether Alan's signature is of Drevicia's line is not yet settled."
"Dravishk, a dragon and Drevicia's sibling, is the Library's hidden enemy and saboteur."
"The Mamoria and the Unisceros are peoples who come to threaten the whole universe."
"Milaro is an elf king with an empire of his own, and Links's oldest friend."
"Milaro is kind and grandfatherly, and becomes the Librarian's mentor."
"Milaro gives the Library Malachite shards by the hundred thousand."
"Malakai is Milaro's grandson, tall, who can turn invisible."
"Malakai becomes the Librarian's friend and, in time, her partner."
"Dottie is a small bench, a superellux futora, who runs the check-in desk."
"Dottie fusses over the Librarian and spreads a warm glow of good feeling."
"Cook is the kitchen golem, who knows what dish a mood needs."
"Cook makes cinnamon doughnuts."
"Aradie is a night owl with black iridescent feathers who sends images to the Librarian."
"Aradie rides the Librarian's shoulder."
"Jim and Bob are the Aracnio brothers, Library Assistants who work the check-in desk."
"Harish and Siliqua are researchers who cleanse Links's infected systems."
"Siliqua is a wood elf."
"Cadre is a four-foot gecko-like calculator of magic, excitable and precise to the decimal."
"Misha is a silver supervisory golem, short and strong, who warps from place to place."
"Eric keeps the fine ledger and cackles with glee over a new fine."
"Geneva is a small winged sprite with gossamer wings."
"Betty is a sprite and the Library's book doctor."
"Nishpa is a Furionas fae healer who runs the hospital wing."
"Hal is a dragon who sends satyrs to the Library for training."
"Drukala, Drivok and Dronar are dragons, Drevicia's kin."
"Jasper is a friend to the Librarian who knows rituals."
"Carafax was a chronicler whose journals hint at truths without saying them."
"The Bectiwode are a beetle-like people the size of a Great Dane, who chitter as they speak."
"The Dabilian are a people with a home world where a mimic chest guards a lost Library book."
"A mimic is a monster disguised as furniture, which can snap a head off."
